  "prefLabel": "Alc 103.02 Responsibilities of the Board",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Alc 103.02 Responsibilities of the Board. The board’s responsibilities shall include:\n\n(a) The criteria for the issuance, reinstatement, and renewal of licenses to applicants qualified under RSA 330-C, Alc 300, and Alc 400 to be LADCs ;\n\n(b) The criteria for the issuance, reinstatement, and renewal of licenses to applicants qualified under RSA 330-C, Alc 300, and Alc 400 to be LCSs;\n\n(c) The criteria for the issuance of certificates to applicants qualified under RSA 330-C, Alc 300, and Alc 400 to be CRSWs;\n\n(d) The criteria for the approval of continuing education programs and providers of such programs; and\n\n(e) Disciplinary proceedings and disciplinary actions against licensees and certificate holders.\n\nSource. #8169, eff 9-21-04; ss by 9417, eff 3-14-09; ss by #14585, eff 6-1-26",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/alc100-500.html"
